.TH MCP-SERVER-PATREON 1 "November 2026" "mcp-server-patreon 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-server-patreon \- MCP server for the Patreon API over stdio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-server-patreon
.RB [\|\-\-version \|]
.RB [\|\-\-help \|]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-server-patreon
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives an LLM agent read-only
access to the Patreon API v2: the authenticated user's profile, campaigns
with tiers, campaign members and posts, with cursor-based pagination.
.PP
It speaks MCP over standard input and output and is normally started by an
MCP client or by mcprack rather than by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATREON_ACCESS_TOKEN
Patreon creator access token (required). Never passed as a tool parameter.
.TP
.B TRANSPORT
MCP transport, default \fBstdio\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/mcp-server-patreon/server.json
mcprack environment-variable manifest.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcprack (1)
.SH AUTHOR
